    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes along with the full build.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change adds a `checkDigit` field \u2014 the Luhn check digit over the digits of `customerCode` \u2014 to the owner response. Since the acceptance test creates an owner and then **GETs** it, the value had to appear on the GET response, so the natural place is the DTO mapper (which serves every read path), not a single create-time responder.\n\nThree small, low-coupling touches:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `checkDigit` schema property (`integer`, 0\u20139, read-only), so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the field and setter.\n\n2. **New `CheckDigit.java`** \u2014 a tiny stateless helper (`Integer of(String)`) that computes the Luhn digit over the code's digits, doubling from the rightmost, returning `null` when the code is absent (mirroring the null-safe `MembershipNumber` helper). All the new complexity lives here, in a class with no surrounding context.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one added `@Mapping` line delegating to `CheckDigit.of(owner.getCustomerCode())`, alongside the existing derived-field mappings.\n\nStructural impact stayed minimal: no existing method body was grown, and the only edited functions are the interface's `toOwnerDto` (one annotation line, CC 1, negligible `WMC_other`) \u2014 the algorithm sits in a fresh cohesive unit rather than inside a large responder method. Full build: **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
